Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(prim3): teach an HQ or B1 cell as the plan's 12 ft
 (3.6576 m) and name the 3.54 m rule tile apart (W5)

The Equity Uprise HQ and both B1 variants told learners "3.54 m/tile". Their
level module lays the building plan at 12 ft a cell and draws the level at
WORLD_M = 12 ft = 3.6576 m a cell; 3.54 m is the shared tactical-rule tile
(TILE_M), 3.2% smaller (the cell is 3.3% larger). The frame shown above every HQ and B1 question now
says both, separately: one cell is 12 ft (3.6576 m) on the building plan;
tactical rules use the separate 3.54 m game tile. Transit / Relay, the
generated operation, the courtyard and the City keep their frames.

Only display text changes. The evaluator, the expected answers, the
feedback and hint strings that signed evidence replays, and the
prim3.lattice-learning/v1 context are unchanged, so existing sessions
replay as before.

The new parity test reads FRAME, WORLD_M, TILE_M, FT and FT_PER_TILE from
the Transit, HQ and B1 level modules and checks each authored square
frame's origin, cell scale and rule tile against them, and that every
question shows the frame. It fails on the PR head (the HQ frame names
3.54 m/tile as the cell) and passes here. docs/prim3/TOPOLOGY-LEARNING.md
records the two scales.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
